    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d386">

                <pb facs="0565" n="491" sameAs="frus:frus1866p1/pg491"/>

                <head>Mr. F. W. Seward to Mr.
                        Williams</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 24.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <hi
                                rendition="#italic">Washington,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1866-02-24"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >February</hi> 24, 1866.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I transmit to you a copy of a note of the
                    21st instant, which has been addressed to this department by Mr. De Figaniere é
                    Morao, the diplomatic representative of Portugal, accredited to this government,
                    who has been directed by his government to ask the co-operation of the United
                    States minister at Peking, with that of the Portuguese minister at that place,
                    in bringing to a satisfactory conclusion any negotiations now pending or which
                    may arise between Portugal and China.</p>
                <p>You are accordingly instructed to lend such assistance as may be in your power,
                    in order to accomplish the desired result.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>F. W. SEWARD, <hi rendition="#italic">Acting
                    Secretary.</hi></signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">S. Wells Williams</hi>, Esq., <hi
                            rendition="#italic">&amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>


                <xi:include href="d386-a1.xml" xpointer="d386-a1"/>
